1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:03,134
The first thing we hear Jesus preach in Matthew is a blessing:

2
00:00:03,529 --> 00:00:19,377
"Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven" And that phrase – the kingdom of heaven – will become one of the defining themes of Matthew’s Gospel. In fact, it appears Thirty-two times throughout the book. When Jesus begins his public ministry, his message is clear:

3
00:00:19,643 --> 00:00:28,909
"Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is near." The kingdom of heaven is Matthew’s way of describing God’s reign, and in this book that reign arrives in person.

